  },
  {
    "insert": "\nThe motivation should explain to the reader why the chosen topic is relevant and which weakness the thesis wants to address. Although the problem is mentioned in the motivation, further explanation of the problem and its consequences is missing. If the reader does not understand why the problem is important or what its implications are, the motivation for the thesis may be weakened. Try to explain the problem and its consequences in more detail."
  },
  {
    "insert": "\n",
    "attributes": {
      "list": "bullet"
    }
  },
  {
    "insert": "The state of the art should present your work in comparison to existing research. While the exposé highlights the potential of LLMs, the weaknesses of the current state of the art and the existing gap should be explained in more detail. This is important to clearly demonstrate the novelty and relevance of your work. Try to complement your SOTA with current weaknesses and thereby try to show which research gaps still exist."
  },
